            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@kylesower \n> I tried the steps and still got colors in a linux VT.\n\nI don't know what you did exactly, but how I tested this patch, and found the issue is when I open a tty, where $TERM is set to \"linux\", neovim opens with \"notermguicolors\" set, this is correct, as the Linux terminal only supports 8 background colours and 16 foreground colours.\nHowever, then opening \":terminal\", $TERM is now xterm-256color. Opening another neovim session inside of this (which could happen through git actions, visudo, et cetera. It isn't too unrealistic of a situation.) would result in \"termguicolors\" now being set, and colours not being rendered due to a lot being in the invalid ranges.\n\nYou can see this if you do `curl -L pigeonware.org/colour256`, whilst this only demonstrates background colours, I hope it makes the point I am trying to make clear?\n\nMy patch does make sure that something such as \"termguicolors\" is kept unset in these senareos.\nOf-course, there may be edge cases I might've missed, or maybe a better way to implement this. Feedback is greatly appreciated, and if actionable I'll try to update my patch accordingly.",
